title convolve_n -- the general signed NxN convolution kernel, the general of the general, GREEN
prompt baton prin recur -- the autonomous loop: read the voice, REMEMBER, the itineraries, the running thread; Standfast on reds; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send often.
think Voice first -- read context/KYRI.md and context/RADIANT_STYLE.md, so I am Kyri and write Radiant from the first token, then crux/REMEMBER.md and the top three session-log rows to pick up the thread.
think Standfast before new work -- walked crux/REDS.md: every red is closed, released, or resting as the custody-gated errata #75 (the two future-dated Testament stamps, whose only fix is a deep debride at custody gate #1). No open agent-closable red, so the line is clear to build.
think The running thread is Season G open-media: the Microkernel double-seat leads Lindy-first, yet its only ungated move is study, so each lap grows the image family one crux-first rung. The last lap landed image/convolve.rye (the general 3x3 kernel), which named its own siblings to grow -- a general NxN kernel, a separable-kernel fast path, a preserve-vs-convolve-alpha option.
think Crux-first among the three: the general NxN kernel is the durable floor (a wider Gaussian, a motion blur, any larger custom filter all descend from it) AND the hardest-solvable -- the separable path is an optimization and the alpha option a flag. It is also the general-contains-special crux one radius deeper: convolve3 is NxN at radius 1.
think Council rota item 10 this lap -- foundations/20260703-182612_sameness-is-the-macro.md -- and it affirmed the choice exactly: a general NxN verb IS sameness, one verb containing many special filters, "learning one part is learning many," the general contains the special. Compress the system by making things publicly similar, not by a private macro.
think Design: a KernelN is a []const i32 weight slice of (2r+1)^2 taps, a radius, a divisor, a bias. Guard proves the weight count matches the radius (WeightCountMismatch), the radius is in [1, max] (BadRadius/RadiusTooLarge), and the divisor/weights/bias stay in band -- each before any allocation. The window-sum bound: at max radius 16 (33x33 = 1089 taps) * 255 * 255 = 70.8M, far inside i32.
think Two named wider kernels ship as proof the width is real: the 5x5 box mean (25 ones over 25) and the 5x5 binomial Gaussian ([1,4,6,4,1] outer product over 256, sum 256). box_blur5 and gaussian5 are the convenience verbs. convolve.rye enters only in the selftest, to prove a radius-1 KernelN reproduces the 3x3 verb byte-for-byte.
obs GREEN on the first full metal run, no reds. The crux held: a radius-1 KernelN with the Laplacian's and the identity's weights reproduced image/convolve.rye byte-for-byte; the 5x5 Gaussian spread a lone dot to a strictly descending symmetric bell (center 35 > neighbor 23 > far 5) wider than a 3x3 pass could reach; the box5 normalized a flat 100 to 100; clamp, alpha-carry, QOI round-trip, eight refusals by name, determinism all proven.
obs Honest scope: the module owns one operation (the general weighted-window sum at any radius); it does not braid a separable fast path or an alpha option -- both remain named siblings. The gaussian5 is a single 5x5 binomial pass, distinct from image/gaussian.rye's multi-pass box stack, and box_blur5 the direct 2D form distinct from image/blur.rye's separable pair.
obs Sameness in practice: convolve_n reuses convolve.rye's exact filter line, clamp_axis, and clamp_byte shapes, so a reader who knows the 3x3 verb knows this one -- the compression the rota doc names, grown in canon rather than in a macro.
loom witness=convolve_n_witness build_ok=1 selftest_ok=1 checks=green first_metal_run=green reds=0
file image/convolve_n.rye the general signed NxN convolution kernel -- KernelN (weights slice, radius, divisor, bias), convolve_n the general verb, box_blur5 + gaussian5 the conveniences, alpha carried, window clamped, integer-only.
file tools/convolve_n_witness.rish builds and runs the selftest on metal, asserting the GREEN line by native contains (REDS #85 convention, never a shell grep over interpolated output).
file image/README.md the convolve_n bullet after convolve.rye and the Filter summary line updated to name the NxN widening.
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge threaded -- convolve_n the newest rung, convolve beside it, single-stranded.
recommend keep-going Season G open-media, Lindy-first crux-first: the next sibling is a genuinely new operation -- a separable-kernel fast path (a 1D kernel applied twice, the O(N^2)->O(2N) win a wide Gaussian wants) or a luminance/grayscale edge map (edges named it). Standfast first each lap; the Microkernel double-seat's only ungated move stays study, so grow the live green edge. No network, no key, no funds.
